# Checks a cell is allowed to fail: an upstream defect in that application
# release on that PHP. Anything not listed
# here still fails the cell. A listed check that passes is reported, so a row can
# be dropped once upstream (or the matrix) moves on.
#
# One row per check: app, set, PHP version, then the check's name exactly as the
# suite prints it, then " -- " and why. `appsets.py check` refuses a row whose
# (app, set, php) is not a cell in tests/apps/sets. The CLI suites
# (tests/apps/cli-lib.sh) honor this file; the HTTP suites do not read it.
#
# app        set   php   check -- why
